  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "3592318df3e06a4b10c8e5c6a4a1a09f81e8d691",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1075666745,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> `WTAP_NSTIME_SECS_MAX`\n\nProbably something more like `WTAP_NSTIME_32BIT_SECS_MAX`, as it's not the maximum number of seconds, it's the maximum possible (positive) value of `secs` that will fit in a 32-bit integer.  If `secs` is 64-bit, that maximum value is 2^32-1, as 2^31-1 will fit in a 64-bit signed or unsigned value; if `secs` is 32-bit, then, if `secs` is signed (as it *probably* is on all platforms on which we run, but that's not guaranteed), it's 2^31-1, otherwise it's 2^32-1.\n\nI think I've seen some tricky expression to determine that; I'll see if I can find it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-24T08:58:27.881Z",
